# Drizzle records sha256(file bytes) for each applied migration in
# drizzle.__drizzle_migrations. Migrations are applied from Linux (CI/deploy),
# so those hashes are of LF content. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites them to CRLF, changing every hash and making `npm run db:status`
# report dozens of already-applied migrations as "edited after it was applied".
# Pin these files to LF so the bytes on disk match the bytes that were hashed.
drizzle/**/*.sql text eol=lf
drizzle/meta/*.json text eol=lf
